# Selecting priority levels with alternative rules
#
# Alice holds a gold level, Bob bronze and Carol platinum. Two rules give
# priority to gold and to platinum, two alternatives for one conclusion. A
# third rule marks as ordinary anyone with a level who has no priority, so
# Alice and Carol have priority and Bob is ordinary. It shows alternative
# rules and a scoped absence test (log:notIncludes) for the remaining case.

@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .
@prefix : <http://example/> .

:alice :level "gold" .
:bob :level "bronze" .
:carol :level "platinum" .

# Gold and platinum each give priority.
{
    ?x :level "gold"
} => {
    ?x :priority true
} .

{
    ?x :level "platinum"
} => {
    ?x :priority true
} .

# Anyone else with a level is ordinary.
{
    ?x :level ?level .
    ?SCOPE log:notIncludes {
        ?x :priority true
    }
} => {
    ?x :ordinary true
} .
